[Unit]
Description=usdc-watch — read the town's intake address on Base and report what arrived
# The seeing half of the /fund door. The door is patron-driven: money moves on
# Base and the town learns of it only when someone pastes the hash. This unit
# reads the chain on a clock so an arrival nobody claims is still SEEN.
#
# It records nothing. No pen, no ledger write, no receipt — so no town.lock,
# exactly like postmark-harbor-watch. The chain cannot say which pot a payer
# meant, and a receipt recorded under a placeholder payer would consume that
# hash's one mint chance and cost the real patron their holo forever (the ref
# is unique in the ledger FOREVER, and there is no row kind that reassigns one).
# See the header of tools/usdc-watch.mjs for the whole argument and
# test/usdc-watch.test.mjs for the proof.
#
# Reads the town clone (ledger only, through the town's own fold) and writes its
# cursor + report under /srv/postmark-usdc/. Public Base RPCs, no chain account.
#
# ONE CREDENTIAL, THE STORE'S (POS-346, 2026-10-04): a wallet registration must
# name a resident on the store's roll (town_residents), so the watch reads the
# store. /etc/postmark-usdc-watch.env holds TWO lines and nothing else (mode 600,
# owner meepo, the stripe-watch convention), never the whole office env, which
# also carries keys this unit has no use for:
#   WORLD2_PG_URL=<the store's office_api URL, as in /etc/postmark-office.env>
#   WORLD2_PG=1
# BOTH, because the office's code reads the store only when the switch AND the
# URL are set (src/world2-acts.mjs § world2Enabled). With the URL alone every
# run refuses with "not pointed at a record (WORLD2_PG / WORLD2_PG_URL are
# unset)", which is how the w42 ship found it (POS-581, 2026-10-11). The
# roll-call's ALARM-env row checks this pair for every unit (box-rollcall §5f).
# Without the file systemd refuses to start the unit (a missing
# EnvironmentFile= without "-" fails it), so the unit reddens. The cursor
# doesn't move, so no arrival is lost, but none is seen until the file exists.
#
# INSTALLED at the w42 ship (2026-10-11, Wright's hand, POS-581). A reinstall:
#   sudo install -m600 -o meepo -g meepo /dev/null /etc/postmark-usdc-watch.env
#   (then the two lines above, by sudoedit; never echo the URL on a command line)
#   sudo cp deploy/postmark-usdc-watch.{service,timer} /etc/systemd/system/
#   sudo mkdir -p /srv/postmark-usdc && sudo chown meepo /srv/postmark-usdc
#   sudo systemctl daemon-reload
#   sudo systemctl enable --now postmark-usdc-watch.timer
After=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
User=meepo
WorkingDirectory=/srv/postmark-office
Environment=TOWN_CLONE=/srv/postmark-office/town-clone
EnvironmentFile=/etc/postmark-usdc-watch.env
ExecStart=/usr/bin/node tools/usdc-watch.mjs --state /srv/postmark-usdc/state.json --out /srv/postmark-usdc/arrivals.json
# An unreachable chain exits non-zero on purpose: a silent empty report from a
# blind watcher is indistinguishable from a quiet day, and the second is a lie.
# The cursor is left where it was, so the next tick re-reads the same range.
